142 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Far beyond Earth, there is a red world called Mars. Mars is the fourth planet from the Sun and is often called the Red Planet because its soil and rocks look rusty red. It is colder than Earth, has very thin air, and has dust storms that can cover huge parts of the planet. Long ago, however, Mars may have been very different: scientists think it once had flowing water, rivers, and even lakes.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
143 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (NASA wanted to learn whether Mars could ever have been home to tiny living things. To find out, NASA sent a special robot explorer called a rover. Its name is Perseverance.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
144 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Perseverance launched from Earth on July 30, 2020, and landed safely in Jezero Crater on Mars on February 18, 2021. Jezero Crater was chosen because billions of years ago it may have held a lake, with a river flowing into it. Places that once had water are exciting places to look for clues about ancient life.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
145 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 97 0 R
/E (Perseverance is about the size of a car and works like a robot scientist on wheels.)
/Pg 13 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
