196 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (Long ago, Jezero Crater on Mars was a very different place. Instead of the dry and dusty land we see today, it once had a large lake filled with water. Rivers flowed into this lake, carrying sand, mud and tiny pieces of rock. Over time, these materials formed a fan-shaped structure called a river delta.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 103 0 R
/E (NASA selected Jezero Crater as the landing site for the Perseverance rover because scientists believed this area could hold clues about the ancient history of Mars. The lake may have provided suitable conditions for tiny living organisms called microbes.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
198 0 obj
<<
