209 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 104 0 R
/E (The surface of Mars is covered with dust, sand, small stones and broken rocks. This loose material is called regolith. Some rocks have small holes, while others have smooth surfaces. Scientists use NASA's Perseverance Rover to study the soil and rocks on Mars. The rover collects rock and soil samples to learn about the planet's past. Scientists have also found some rocks that may contain signs of tiny living things from long ago. By studying the soil and land, scientists can understand how Mars looked in the past and whether life may have existed there.)
/Pg 20 0 R
/K [5]
