/P 107 0 R
/E (Ingenuity was a small robotic helicopter that travelled to Mars attached to NASA's Perseverance rover in February 2021. It was designed to test whether powered and controlled flight was possible in the extremely thin Martian atmosphere. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
227 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 107 0 R
/E (On 19 April 2021, Ingenuity made history by completing the first powered flight on another planet. Originally planned for just five flights as a technology demonstration, it far exceeded expectations by completing 72 flights. It also captured aerial images of the Martian surface, helping the Perseverance team explore and plan rover movements. However, its flying mission came to an end in January 2024 after a rotor blade was damaged. Ingenuity proved that aerial exploration is possible on Mars and opened new possibilities for future space missions.)
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
