/Title (Before Perseverance began its journey to Mars, NASA engineers carefully prepared the spacecraft's landing components at the Kennedy Space Center in Florida. On May 4, 2020, the backshell-powered descent vehicle and entry vehicle assemblies were being prepared for attachment to the rover. The cone-shaped backshell held the parachute, which would help slow the spacecraft during its descent. Along with the heat shield, it protected the rover and descent stage as they travelled through the Martian atmosphere. Every component was carefully designed and assembled to help Perseverance reach the surface safely.)
/Dest [22 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 7 0 R
/Prev 579 0 R
/Next 548 0 R
